        "v": 5,
        "title": "Allow underscore aliases for spawned agent IDs",
        "summary": "Added normalizeAgentIdForLookup to treat underscores as hyphens in agent name segments. Agent registry and spawn handlers now resolve IDs using this normalization, enabling flexible matching for local templates, database caches, and spawn permissions. Publisher IDs and versions remain case-sensitive and unnormalized.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T00:31:36.792Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you tell the system to start an agent, you can now type the agent's name with underscores in place of hyphens and it will still find the right one. For example, if the agent's real name uses hyphens like \"my-agent\", you can now write \"my_agent\" and the system will treat them the same when looking it up. This only works for the agent name itself; the publisher and version parts stay exactly as typed.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "6cf48a5c7cad",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:47:22.263Z"
