        "v": 5,
        "title": "Kimi K2.6 replaces GLM 5.1 as free default model",
        "summary": "Kimi K2.6 replaces GLM 5.1 as the free model for base2, editor-lite, and code-reviewer-lite agents. The CLI model selector and session hooks now reference FREEBUFF_KIMI_MODEL_ID, updating quota and fallback logic examples. Model type definitions in agent-definition.ts remove kimi-k2.5 and add kimi-k2.6. Common constants switch from FREEBUFF_MODELS to SUPPORTED_FREEBUFF_MODELS for validation.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T00:31:56.999Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The free coding helper that kicks in when you don't pick a premium model has swapped brains today - it now runs on Kimi K2.6 instead of the old GLM 5.1. If you're using the editor or code reviewer in light/free mode, or the base agent when you don't choose a paid model, you're now talking to Kimi K2.6. The model picker in the command-line menu shows Kimi 2.6 as your default free option alongside the existing Gemini 3.1 Pro, and the system that decides which model backs which agent has dropped references to the older Kimi K2.5 and GLM names. This is live now - anyone running the CLI or using the free-tier agents gets Kimi 2.6 automatically.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
