      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "CLI model picker shows rate limits and simplifies navigation",
        "summary": "The CLI freebuff model selector now displays 'Used today' and 'Limit used' hints by fetching per-model quota snapshots via a new `rateLimitsByModel` field in the session state. Navigation logic was refactored to remove selectable-filtering from `nextFreebuffModelId`, allowing users to arrow through all models and rely on the picker's `isJoinable` check to prevent joining exhausted queues. This change spans `cli/src/components/freebuff-model-selector.tsx`, `common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts`, and `web/src/server/free-session/public-api.ts`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T00:32:02.438Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you open the model picker in the command-line tool, each model now shows a small badge telling you how much of your daily or per-session quota you've already used for that specific model, so you can see upfront whether it's already exhausted before you pick it. Navigation was cleaned up so your arrow keys move through every model in the list rather than skipping over ones that look unavailable, and the picker decides in real time which ones you can actually join based on live quota data fetched from the server. The live quota data now includes a new rate-limits-by-model snapshot that the picker reads to display those per-model exhaustion hints, and this is already in place and active today.",
